  "question": {
    "text": "If wavelength of the first line of the Paschen series of hydrogen atom is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>720</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>, then the wavelength of the second line of this series is _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>nm</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "492",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Paschen series are spectral lines coming to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>st</mi></msup></math> line of Paschen series makes a transition from, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math> line&nbsp;of Paschen series makes a transition from, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>We know that,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>1</mn><mi>st</mi></msup></math> line,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>and for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>nd</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;line,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>R</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><msup><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>720</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>720</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>175</mn><mn>256</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>or&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mn>720</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>175</mn><mn>256</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#955;</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8776;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>492</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math></p>"
  }
}